{"cluster_id": "C-1683", "topic": "condemned-summary-seal", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B010-099", "B011-014"], "canonical_claim": "Every new fold seal contains a `condemned_summary` total over shards `0..gc_shards-1`; folding computes it from written condemned rows, while pure-carry shards copy the parent's entry verbatim. Additionally, `CasFoldSeal` contains a per-GC-shard `condemned_summary` with `condemned_total`, `pending_total`, and `oldest_nonpending_condemn_round`, where `UINT64_MAX` means no nonpending condemned row.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-10-cas-retired-in-snapshot.md#task-4-seal-summary-round-wiring-graduationdue", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-10-cas-retired-in-snapshot-design.md#seal-summary"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1684", "topic": "graduation-due-summary", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B010-101", "B010-102"], "canonical_claim": "For `snap_generation == 0`, `graduationDue` returns false; otherwise it reads the adopted seal and fails closed by returning true when the seal is missing, undecodable, or its summary is not total over `gc_shards`. Additionally, When the adopted seal summary is valid, `graduationDue` is true exactly when some shard has `pending_total > 0` or `oldest_nonpending_condemn_round < current_round`; it requires no backend GET beyond the seal read.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-10-cas-retired-in-snapshot.md#task-4-seal-summary-round-wiring-graduationdue"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1685", "topic": "GC rebuild must first traverse journals and accumulate per-shard deltas ", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B010-107"], "canonical_claim": "GC rebuild must first traverse journals and accumulate per-shard deltas and `edge_bearing`, then list physical blobs and head zero-edge bodies, mint condemned rows, append them to shard runs, seal summaries, and only then CAS `gc/state`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-10-cas-retired-in-snapshot.md#task-6-rebuild-reorder-blob-list-before-run-flush-condemned-rows-in-rebuilt-runs"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1686", "topic": "`RetiredMergeResult` remains the interface for `graduated`, `spared`, `r", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B011-023"], "canonical_claim": "`RetiredMergeResult` remains the interface for `graduated`, `spared`, `redelete`, and `replaced` outcomes, which continue to drive outcome logs, `.meta` transitions, B170 events, and `entries_condemned`, `entries_graduated`, and `entries_redeleted` counters.", "issue_ids": ["B170"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-10-cas-retired-in-snapshot-design.md#merge"]}
