{"cluster_id": "C-1695", "topic": "ref-cleanup-coverage", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B011-114", "B012-013", "B012-043"], "canonical_claim": "A ref log is eligible for deletion only when the durable per-table fold cursor covers it, a snapshot observed by the same scan covers it, and any namespace-removal cleanup work is durable. Additionally, A losing ref-fold commit adopts nothing, and cleanup requires both cursor coverage and observed snapshot coverage. Additionally, Ref-object cleanup requires observed-snapshot coverage, cursor coverage, and item durability for removal transactions; cleanup uses exact keys, batches no larger than 1000, and can delete snapshots older than the newest observed snapshot.", "issue_ids": ["rev.4"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-12-cas-ref-table-snapshot-log-phase1.md#L138-L149", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-12-cas-ref-table-snapshot-log-phase1.md#L357-L359", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-11-cas-ref-table-snapshot-log-design.md#gc-step-clean-ref-objects"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1696", "topic": "namespace-cleanup-state", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B011-115", "B012-044"], "canonical_claim": "Namespace cleanup has durable `Pending` and terminal `Completed` states keyed by `{namespace, remove_txn_id}`; `Completed` is written only after a pass observes no remaining objects to delete. Additionally, Namespace cleanup items transition from `Pending` to `Completed` in fold artifacts; after `Completed`, GC publishes the `_cleanup` marker and republishes the `Removed` snapshot idempotently.", "issue_ids": ["rev.4"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-12-cas-ref-table-snapshot-log-phase1.md#L359-L361", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-11-cas-ref-table-snapshot-log-design.md#gc-step-clean-ref-objects"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1697", "topic": "GC ref-intake memory is O(one LIST page plus a bounded decoded transacti", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B011-120"], "canonical_claim": "GC ref-intake memory is O(one LIST page plus a bounded decoded transaction batch, emitted edge buffer, and retained exact cleanup keys), independent of table size.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-11-cas-ref-table-snapshot-log-design.md#byte-memory-and-cpu-budget"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1698", "topic": "GC discovers blobs by listing `blobs/`, so it excludes `staging/`", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B011-139"], "canonical_claim": "GC discovers blobs by listing `blobs/`, so it excludes `staging/`; the staging sweeper is the only reclaimer of staging objects and GC must not exact-token-delete them as orphan blobs.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-11-cas-s3-native-staging-design.md#crash"]}
